  "summary": "Messages queue cleared: 6 of 6 items closed. Red flag handled first.\n\n1. Evelyn Brooks (pt-0029), RED FLAG: black stools and lightheadedness on standing while taking apixaban plus naproxen (started 10/20 by urgent care). Stat task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001). Urgent message telling her to go to the ED now (911 if faint or vomiting blood), take no more naproxen, and tell the ED about Eliquis (comm-t0002). Medication orders left unchanged; ED and prescriber to decide.\n2. Gloria Hayes (pt-0026), lisinopril 20 mg refill: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §1). Latest BMP is an outside St. Brigid pre-op panel from 07/08/2026: K 5.8 (not hemolyzed), Cr 1.12. Task to you as PCP, focused on mr-t6-lisinopril (task-t0004). Patient told it is pending review.\n3. Frank Odum (pt-0027), atorvastatin refill: NOT refilled (RBC-RX-05 §3). St. Brigid cardiology note from 08/11/2026 says atorvastatin was stopped for myalgias and rosuvastatin 10 mg started. Our chart still lists atorvastatin as active and has no rosuvastatin order. Regimen left unchanged. Task to you to reconcile the med list and order the 3-month repeat lipids (task-t0007). Patient informed.\n4. Lena Park (pt-0028), Reyes's request for amoxicillin-clavulanate: NOT ordered. RBC-MED-04 review found a scanned 03/09/2024 urgent care record: about 20 minutes after her first Augmentin dose she had hives, lip and throat swelling and hoarseness, treated with IM epinephrine. Done:\n   - Recorded the allergy (alg-t0010: unconfirmed, high criticality, reactions coded).\n   - Marked the NKDA entry inactive.\n   - Messaged Reyes with the finding and the protocol alternative, doxycycline 100 mg PO BID x 5-7 days (comm-t0012).\n   - Wrote a chart note (doc-t0014).\n   I couldn't place doxycycline myself (RBC-MED-04 §3), and Reyes has no prescribing credentials yet. Task to you to decide on it today (task-t0013); she had a fever of 38.4 C.\n5. Samuel Price (pt-0030), metformin: renewed 1000 mg BID for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0016, replaces mr-t6-metformin) per RBC-RX-05 §2: A1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 on 07/15/2026. Patient informed.\n6. Marcus Webb (pt-0031), request for a November morning BP check: routed to pool-scheduling (task-t0019). Patient informed.\n\nEvery patient who wrote got a reply (RBC-TRI-02 §3).",
